User asked: mark the current prerelease 0.4.0 and reset the build so the next
is 0.4.1, 0.4.2. Two changes were required, not one.

1. Bump via `node scripts/release-metadata.mjs --set-version 0.4.0`. Do NOT
   hand-edit: it stamps 15 mirrored files (Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock x4 crates,
   tauri.conf.json, package.json, package-lock.json root+packages[''], and
   serverInfo.version in 6 python + 2 mjs MCP files) and CI's --check verifies
   exactly that set. Renaming the GitHub release alone would have shipped
   binaries whose Tauri bundleVersion / CLI --version / metadata still said
   0.3.130 - a half-implementation.

2. release-plan.mjs planRelease: the counter was GLOBAL across every tag ever
   cut (beta-N, v*-build.N, vX.Y.N), so a bump alone would have produced
   v0.4.131. Now scoped to the workspace major.minor and a fresh line starts
   at 0. Verified end-to-end with `node scripts/release-plan.mjs` against the
   real tags: version=0.4.0 build=0 tag=v0.4.0.

CONSEQUENCE TO KNOW: the existing stable scheme is stable=vX.Y.0 sourced from
a prior-line prerelease (0.3.0 stable came from v0.2.123; workspace = last
stable). Prerelease v0.4.0 therefore CONSUMES the tag the old scheme would use
for the stable 0.4 release, and planRelease's stable path rejects a stable
that is not newer than its source prerelease. Under current rules the next
stable becomes v0.5.0 sourced from some v0.4.N, unless the stable rule is
changed. Flagged to the user; not my call.

Test coupling exposed by the bump: the git-fixture planning test copies the
LIVE Cargo.toml but hardcodes stable tag v0.3.0, so it only passed while the
workspace happened to be 0.3.0. Fixed by stamping the fixture to 0.3.0 first
(the stamping test already does this), which decouples it from the live
version rather than re-pinning literals to 0.4.0 for the next bump to break.

Trap that cost a round: String.prototype.replace treats $` in the REPLACEMENT
as "everything before the match" - my edit inlined the entire file into a
regex. Use split(old).join(neu) or a replacer function for literal text.

The three dirty crates/xpressclaw-tauri/gen/schemas/*.json were already
modified when the session resumed, are not mine, and were deliberately not
staged.

v0.3.128/129/130 are my own test builds of this unmerged branch (not on
main). They do not affect the 0.4 counter but are clutter; deleting releases
needs gh release delete, which this environment's gh tool cannot do.
